From 30b80f4658a87d887c4ca9c149305fe80c76bfb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sahil Chaudhari <sahilc@pensando.io>
Date: Thu, 9 Apr 2026 12:05:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add Salina ASIC support

This commit adds comprehensive support for the AMD Pensando Salina ASIC,
a next-generation ARM64-based network processor SoC featuring a 16-core
ARM Neoverse-N1 cluster with GICv3 interrupt controller and ITS (Interrupt
Translation Service) for MSI support.

Device Tree Changes:
- Add Salina ASIC device tree files (salina-asic.dts, salina-asic.dtsi)
- Add 16-core CPU topology configuration (salina-16core.dtsi)
- Add N1-specific common configurations (salina-n1-common.dtsi)
- Add flash partition layout for N1 platforms (salina-n1-flash-parts.dtsi)
- Update Pensando DTS Makefile to build Salina DTB
- Add AMD device tree path for Elba compatibility (amd/elba-*.dtsi)
- Update memory region definitions for mdev support

Interrupt Controller Support:
- Add AMD Pensando MSI encapsulator support to GICv3-ITS driver
  * Allows MSI writes to be directed to custom encapsulator address
  * Essential for Pensando's platform MSI architecture
  * Reads second reg entry from device tree for encapsulator base
- Update IRQ chip Kconfig for Salina interrupt controller dependencies

Reset Controller:
- Add Salina System Resource reset controller driver (reset-salinasr.c)
  * Controls peripheral reset functions via IPC to management processor
  * Management processor is ARM64 A35 in Salina SoC
  * Provides reset control for on-chip peripherals
- Add Kconfig and Makefile entries for Salina reset driver

SoC Platform Support:
- Add ARCH_PENSANDO_SALINA_SOC configuration option
- Restructure Pensando Kconfig as choice between Elba and Salina SoCs
- Add CMN (Coherent Mesh Network) PMU interrupt controller support
  * Enables performance monitoring for interconnect fabric
- Add Salina-specific PCIe controller definitions (cap_pcie_salina.h)
- Update cap_pcie driver for Salina PCIe differences

SPI Driver Enhancement:
- Add Salina-specific SPI controller support to spi-dw-mmio driver
  * Handles Salina's DesignWare SPI controller configuration
  * Required for SPI flash and peripheral access

Device Tree Bindings:
- Add capmem device tree binding header (pensando,capmem.h)
  * Defines constants for capacity memory regions
  * Used for DMA and device memory management

Configuration Updates:
- Update EDAC Kconfig for Salina memory controller support
- Update UIO Kconfig for Salina platform MSI devices

Platform Device Support:
- Update elba-mdev.dtsi with enhanced MSI parent configurations
- Add memory region definitions for network device DMA

This enables complete Salina ASIC functionality including:
- 16-core ARM Neoverse-N1 CPU cluster operation
- GICv3 + ITS hierarchical interrupt management
- Platform MSI support for network and crypto devices
- SPI flash access and peripheral I/O
- PCIe endpoint and root complex operation
- System-level reset and power management
- Performance monitoring infrastructure

Tested on Salina ASIC hardware with kernel 6.1.123.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
